From: KED BSP <bsp@ked.local>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rdkafka_conf.h: honor OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE

Buildroot builds OpenSSL 3 with `no-engine` unless
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBOPENSSL_ENGINES is set, so libcrypto.so.3 does not
export the (deprecated) ENGINE_* symbols. librdkafka enables its
ENGINE support based on the OpenSSL version alone, which produces a
librdkafka.so.1 with a dangling reference to ENGINE_init: any
consumer linked against it (e.g. GStreamer's libgstdxstream.so)
then fails to load with:

  librdkafka.so.1: undefined symbol: ENGINE_init

Gate WITH_SSL_ENGINE on !defined(OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE) as well, and fix
the ssl.engine struct member to use the same WITH_SSL_ENGINE guard
(it used the raw version check, which would not compile once ENGINE
support is disabled). Also include <openssl/opensslconf.h> explicitly
so OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE is visible where the guard is evaluated.

Upstream status: not submitted
---
 src/rdkafka_conf.h | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/rdkafka_conf.h
+++ b/src/rdkafka_conf.h
@@ -33,8 +33,12 @@
 #include "rdlist.h"
 #include "rdkafka_cert.h"
 
+#if WITH_SSL
+#include <openssl/opensslconf.h>
+#endif
+
 #if WITH_SSL && OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x10100000 &&                        \
-    !defined(OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL)
+    !defined(OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL) && !defined(OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE)
 #define WITH_SSL_ENGINE 1
 /* Deprecated in OpenSSL 3 */
 #include <openssl/engine.h>
@@ -257,7 +261,7 @@
                 /** CSV list of Windows certificate stores */
                 char *ca_cert_stores;
                 char *crl_location;
-#if WITH_SSL && OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x10100000
+#if WITH_SSL_ENGINE
                 ENGINE *engine;
 #endif
                 char *engine_location;
